**C1: confirmed, must fix before merge.** Line 19 of `src/orders.ts` is `subtotalCents(order) * (1 - percentOff / 100)`, and nothing rounds the result. Any discount that doesn't divide evenly gives fractional cents: 999 cents at 10% is 999 × 0.9 = 899.1. So the function returns a non-integer amount, which breaks R2 ("Amounts are integer cents, never floating-point numbers"). The 7% float-error example only makes it worse; the 999-cent case is enough on its own.

**C2: confirmed, should fix.** The only discount test is 1000 cents at 10% (line 11 of `src/orders.test.ts`). 1 − 0.1 is exactly 0.9 as a float, so the result is exactly 900 and the test passes. It never hits a non-round result, so it can't catch the C1 bug. It also doesn't test the RangeError for values below 0, above 100, or NaN.

